        <h2>2. Public Domain Scientific Formulas &amp; Academic Attribution</h2>
        <p>The mathematical formulas implemented within our calculation tools (including the classic Quetelet Body Mass Index formula, the Oxford Trefethen 2.5 BMI model, the Mifflin-St Jeor and Harris-Benedict BMR equations, the Boer and Devine ideal body weight formulas, and the Mosteller body surface area equation) are published, peer-reviewed scientific works residing in the public domain or acknowledged academic literature. Real BMI makes no claim of exclusive ownership over these underlying mathematical laws of nature or public health classification cutoffs established by the World Health Organization (WHO) or Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC). Our copyright applies to the original software code, computational user interface, curated instructional text, and proprietary interactive visualizations developed by our team.</p>

